course: dictionary
lesson: 12959
title: Excreting waste
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Living things make waste as they work, and excreting means getting rid of that waste so it does not build up inside the body. «The kidneys excrete waste in urine» tells you the kidneys remove waste and send it out as wee.
explain: «Sweat helps the skin excrete waste when you get hot after running.» Excreting is not the same as eating or breathing in. Look for the clue: excreting always means pushing waste out, never taking something in.
explain: Plants excrete too. They push out waste materials they do not need, so excreting happens even in living things that cannot run or go to the toilet.
fact: Excreting means getting rid of waste from the body, such as urine (wee), faeces (poo) or sweat.
fact: «Excreting waste» is a phrase you will often see in science.
fact: «Excreting through the kidneys» means removing waste from the body in urine.
fact: Excretion is one of the seven life processes of living things, remembered as MRS GREN.
fact: Lungs excrete carbon dioxide, a waste gas that you breathe out.
exercise: «The kidneys excrete waste in urine.» What does excrete mean here? | Move quickly | *Get rid of waste | Make new bones | Take in food
exercise: Plants excrete waste materials they do not need. What does excreting mean for a plant? | Growing taller | *Pushing out waste they do not need | Taking in water | Making their own food
exercise: In MRS GREN, which letter stands for excretion? | R | *E | M | N
test: Which body part excretes waste in urine? | Lungs | *Kidneys | Skin | Heart
test: Why is excreting important for living things? | It makes the body grow taller | It makes them breathe faster | It stops them needing food | *It stops harmful waste building up in the body
exam: Which of these is NOT a way the body excretes waste? | Urine from the kidneys | *Eating a meal | Sweating through the skin | Breathing out carbon dioxide from the lungs
